# GBear naming (not Playnite)

This product is **GBear**. Do not introduce **Playnite**, **playnite**, or **PLAYNITE** in new or edited code, comments, docs, identifiers, filenames, URLs, logs, preferences, or user-visible copy.

## Use

| Kind | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Types / files | `GBearStreamHostManager`, `GBearVideoActivity`, `GBearHID` |
| HTTP | `/gbear/v1/…` |
| Protocol | `gbear-stream/1` |
| Frames | `GBV1` video, `GBA1` / `GBAS` audio, `GBI1` touch, `GBK1` keyboard, `GBG1` gamepad |
| Dart / Kotlin | `GBearHostClient`, `gbearStreamDebug`, `com.gbear.companion` |

```swift
// ❌ BAD
PlayniteStreamControlServer()
POST "/playnite/v1/stream/start"

// ✅ GOOD
GBearStreamControlServer()
POST "/gbear/v1/stream/start"
```

## Allowed leftovers

Only when migrating data that already shipped to devices:

- Android `deleteNotificationChannel` IDs
- Moving `~/Library/Application Support/GBear/playnite-stream` → `gbear-stream`

Do not add new Playnite names for those migrations. Moonlight and Sunshine may appear only as **third-party** vendored projects, never as GBear’s product name.
